.TH tensor-wasm-completions 1  "tensor-wasm-completions " 
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-completions \- Emit shell completion scripts for the named shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm\-completions\fR [\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISHELL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Emit shell completion scripts for the named shell.
.PP
By default the script is written to stdout. Pass `\-\-out\-dir <dir>` to write it to a conventional filename inside `<dir>` instead — used by `crates/tensor\-wasm\-cli/completions/` regeneration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR \fI<OUT_DIR>\fR
Optional output directory. When provided, the script is written to `<dir>/<conventional\-name>` (e.g. `tensor\-wasm.bash`, `_tensor\-wasm` for zsh, `tensor\-wasm.fish`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISHELL\fR>
Target shell (bash, zsh, fish, powershell, elvish)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
